{# The light/dark switch. Rendered in the nav on every page, and again in the
   contents sidebar on essays, where it stays reachable while you read. Both
   copies are driven by the one listener in base.njk, which binds every
   `[data-theme-toggle]` — hence the attribute rather than an id, which can
   only ever match the first. `cls` carries the per-context muting: the nav
   mutes the button itself, while the sidebar is already muted as a whole. #}
{# The nudge: `align-middle` lands the disc's centre 0.24em above the baseline,
   which is below even the x-height centre and reads as sunk. Measured in
   Chrome, the cap-height centre of the 14px sans is 0.36em up, so the icon
   rides 0.19em low. In em, not px, so it holds if the type size changes. #}
{% macro themeToggle(cls = "opacity-50 hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity") %}
<button data-theme-toggle type="button" aria-label="Switch theme"
  class="align-middle relative -top-[0.19em] {{ cls }}">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="1em" height="1em" aria-hidden="true" class="inline">
    <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/>
    <path d="M12 3a9 9 0 0 0 0 18z" fill="currentColor"/>
  </svg>
</button>
{% endmacro %}
